{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Nobleindie","id":"361351593292988425","is_bot":0,"username":"nobleindie"},"author_id":"361351593292988425","channel_id":"638590420254720030","content":"Lilia moves her chair so that she is directly facing Castor. She takes his hand in hers and begins to pray to the Raven Queen. For a moment she feels almost cold, and her bright green eyes go dark. It feels similar to when she summoned her wings the night before, but this time it's much softer. The prayer is in Celestial:","created_at":"2020-08-11T01:47:03.827000Z","edited_at":"2020-08-11T01:48:46.642000Z","id":"742559680097943643","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Nobleindie","id":"361351593292988425","is_bot":0,"username":"nobleindie"},"author_id":"361351593292988425","channel_id":"638590420254720030","content":"|| \"Raven Queen, hear my words. Sir Castor Peirce is missing something he holds dear. The memory of his mother has been taken from him, I believe this memory could have found its way to you in the Fortress of Memories.  You pull memories from those who have left this world to cleanse their souls, I know you also pull memories from the living to preserve their life. Sir Castor feels a hole in his mind, he knows something is missing, in order to preserve his life and to help him fight, I ask of you to lend him his memory. After death it can return to you. I pray to you as the Keeper of Memories to bless this man with a complete mind, he fights for the Gods, and against the Hunger. If he can do so without worrying that his mind isn’t whole, please return his mother to him, for now she can only live in his mind. As the Goddess of Death, please send one of your faithful crows with this gift, for you will be given more after his death and mine.\"||","created_at":"2020-08-11T01:47:29.948000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"742559789657358436","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
